Troendle et al. recently proposed several methods on the use of win time for capturing the overall treatment benefit from an ordered composite endpoint [20]. The appeal of utilizing win time is to better reflect the participant clinical experience, measured in time, as they progress from less severe to more severe clinical events. We focus on one of these methods, the expected win time against reference (EWTR), which first estimates a distribution of clinical states from baseline (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
