The expected outcome under a PTR strategy is the average of the observed outcome for those receiving the recommended treatments, weighted by the probability of being randomized to that group (π). Note that treatment, Z, is effect-coded −1/2 and 1/2 for control and treatment for clearer interpretability [13, 24, 25]. Under non-personalized strategies, the expected outcome under treatment is [4]:7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
