First, training datasets (R = 1000 trials of size N = 1000) were simulated following the above CSH models and effect modification parameter values for each scenario (Fig. 1). For each trial in the training dataset, we transformed the two clinical time-to-event outcomes to an ordered composite endpoint by estimating the clinical state distribution via extended Markov model to derive an EWTR for every participant i. In Kraemer’s moderator analyses the treatment variable was re-parameterized using effect coding, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
