Application of composite moderator framework to the AFFIRM Trial. A Distribution of clinical state probabilities over time using the reference group (rate-control). Probability estimates are based on the extended Markov model. To align with publication results, data were truncated at five years. B Distribution of expected win time against reference (EWTR, in days) by treatment strategy. Dotted vertical line marks the EWTR at zero, indicating no difference in expected time spent in better clinical states relative to the reference. Horizontal boxplots indicate the median and interquartile range for each treatment strategy, with density shading illustrating the distribution of EWTR (in days). C Regression estimates were used to plot predicted EWTR for each treatment strategy across observed values of composite moderator M*, with shaded bands indicating 95% bootstrapped confidence intervals. Regression lines for rate- and rhythm-control cross at the vertical dashed line (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
